# kk-daily-publish3-cn-peak — domestic live window (tasks 0323 R5, 0334 R1-R3; kk news verbs
# since 0369).
#
# Fires at 17:00 local because the audience window is 09:00 Asia/Shanghai and launchd/cron
# intervals follow the MACHINE's zone; the window's own wait node sleeps the remainder, which is
# 1 h from 17:00 PDT and 0 h after the DST flip — so the entry never needs editing twice a year.
#
# Which rows go live is the preset's decision, not this line's (ADR-022 amendment): the shipped
# `daily-ai-voice` preset owns the live/draft matrix for `cn-peak`, so the entry carries no
# `--live-channels`. A live row pauses only with `--live-confirm`; `--unattended` keeps the
# window honest about a gated miss (diagnose, tier-0 repair) instead of silently dropping it.
#
# `kk news publish` owns the LA date math. A crontab command ends at the first UNESCAPED percent
# sign, so an inline `date +%F` would silently truncate the entry; the verb computes dates in
# process. `run_date` is "today" in America/Los_Angeles, which is the day directory the 04:30
# generation wrote.
#
# Rendered by `kk schedule render kk-daily-publish3-cn-peak --platform cron --repo <checkout>`;
# kk never edits the operator's crontab. MERGE, never replace:
#
#     crontab -l > /tmp/kk-cn-peak.cron 2>/dev/null || :
#     kk schedule render kk-daily-publish3-cn-peak --platform cron --repo "$PWD" >> /tmp/kk-cn-peak.cron
#     crontab /tmp/kk-cn-peak.cron
0 17 * * * cd {{repo}} && mkdir -p .works/kk-news-publish && PATH="{{home}}/.bun/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin" TZ=America/Los_Angeles kk news publish --window cn-peak --unattended >> {{repo}}/.works/kk-news-publish/cn-peak.log 2>&1
